---
title: 'Don’t stop at the tiles'
slug: 'dont-stop-at-the-tiles'
date: '2026-09-04'
excerpt: 'The tiles can feel like the finish — Prove is when the verse stays.'
tags: ['doctrinal-mastery', 'student-tip']
author: 'Patrick'
---

Scripture Builder tiles can feel like winning. The phrases click into place, the verse looks right, and it is tempting to call it done.

That pass is real work. It is not the last pass.

**Prove** is where it sticks. Type the verse with first-letter hints. Then type it cold — no prompts, no tiles to lean on. That is the moment you know you know it.

Stay with the same verse until you can produce the words without the board. Mastery is not the tiles looking finished. It is the doctrine coming back when you need it.
